    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9c104d33-ed3c-5e5a-b2bb-e3ee4bf6fede",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "What is the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)$ without using a calculator?\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $\\frac{\\pi}{12}=\\frac{\\pi}{3}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.*",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $\\frac{\\pi}{12}=\\frac{\\pi}{3}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nRecall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y)=\\sin x\\cos y-\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right) &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
